  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law and the insurance law, in relation to\nrequiring space for donate life registration in the initial process of setting\nup an online member service portal with an insurer; and to amend a chapter of\nthe laws of 2022 amending the public health law and the insurance law relating\nto requiring space for donate life registration on certain insurance forms, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S. 8805 and A. 10186, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S839",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S839-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§4310 & 4408, Pub Health L; amd §§3216, 3221 & 4306, Ins L; amd §5, Chap of 2022 (as proposed in S.8805 & A.10186)",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S839\n\nSPONSOR: BRESLIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law and the insurance law, in relation\nto requiring space for donate life registration in the initial process\nof setting up an online member service portal with an insurer; and to\namend a chapter of the laws of 2022 amending the public health law and\nthe insurance law relating to requiring space for donate life registra-\ntion on certain insurance forms, as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S. 8805 and A. 10186, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2022,\nc.758, to clarify provisions relating donate life registration opportu-\nnities\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThe changes exclude Medicaid policies from the requirement since the\nfederal government prescribes what types of forms they must provide;\nmake technical amendments; narrow the transaction forms subject to this\nrequirement; expands on the types of insurance policies subject to this\nrequirement; and push the effective date to 18 months to allow an appro-\npriate implementation time.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 758 of the Laws of 2022. 5.8805 and A.10186\nboth passed the Senate and Assembly in May 2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided however that sections\none, two, three, four, and five of this act shall take effect on the\nsame date and in the same manner as a chapter of the laws of 2022 amend-\ning the public health law and the insurance law relating to requiring\nspace for donate life registration on certain insurance forms, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S. 8805 and A. 10186, takes\neffect.\n",
